  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {The dependency direction between the tower and its algebras is currently the OPPOSITE of the intended design, so anyone answering from appearance answers backwards.},
  check    = {standing},
  note     = {kind=finding by=witness-tower. ⚑ MEASURE IT, never infer it from the subtree's name: agda_defs --between Src Dst, and ORDER IS THE QUESTION — running it BOTH ways is how an inversion is measured rather than asserted. --consumers and --depends aggregate to a package COUNT, which says the tower leans on Algebra.F2 but not WHICH modules through WHICH, and only the second form can plan a re-derivation. STANDING until the direction is corrected, at which point this retires with the commit that corrected it. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): currently the OPPOSITE of the intended design, so anyone answering from appearance answers backwards; measure with --between run BOTH ways}
